Summary of the 7 findings:

| # | Severity | Area |
|---|----------|------|
| 1 | **high** | `CC_CV_MARGIN=0.85` is a flat derating applied to the entire charge curve; double-counts CV taper when a charging curve LUT is present (`mod.rs:473`) |
| 2 | **high** | `PowerSetpoint` silently bypasses `bms_ready_by_power` — external controller bears sole responsibility for Ready-By deadlines (`mod.rs:440`) |
| 3 | **high** | `DepartureDeadline` Override sets `power_kw` to force max-rate charging, but `emit_vote` drops it because `departure_hour` takes precedence (`composer.rs:152-161`) |
| 4 | **medium** | `Nightly` strategy omits `DepartureDeadline` — TOU window blocks cannot be overridden by deadline urgency |
| 5 | **medium** | V2L/V2G reuse `charging_efficiency` for DC→AC discharge — no separate `discharge_efficiency` parameter (`mod.rs:640`) |
| 6 | **medium** | V2L/V2G discharge floor ignores pending Ready-By deadline — could compromise departure SOC |
| 7 | **low** | OCHRE has no equivalent multi-strategy priority model for cross-reference |
